        .span9
          section#manage
            .page-header
              h2 Manage templates in a traveler
            p When you want to change the procedure described in a traveler, you will need to update the corresponding template of the traveler. Such a change can be to adjust the sequence of the elements in the template or to add/remove elements. You can always create a new traveler from the updated template, and start from there. However, you might want to update an active traveler that already collected data and notes. The traveler template management feature is designed for this purpose. The owner of a traveler can use a new template in the traveler. S/he can also switch back to a template previously used in the traveler when needed.

            p Click the "Manage templates" button to go to the template manager page for the traveler.

            img(src='#{prefix}/images/config-form.png')
            p The left side of the template manager page has three tables: the active template, the used templates, and the available templates. The right side is a preview of the traveler with the selected template and the data and notes already collected in the traveler. When the page first loaded, the active template is highlighted. The active and used templates table contains template aliases and their last activation date.

            img(src='#{prefix}/images/form-manager.png')

            p The available templates table contains the same set of templates as in the "My templates" tab on the main page of the traveler application. A template will be selected and highlighted when you click the #[i.fa.fa-eye.fa-lg.a-color] icon, and the preview on the right side of the page will be refreshed. A #[i.fa.fa-edit.fa-lg.a-color] icon in the "Reference" column links to the template that was originally based on. You might want to use an updated version of that template to update the traveler. Note that a traveler contains only the snapshot copy of the template when it is used.

          section#add
            .page-header
              h2 Use an available template
            p First locate the template that you want to use in the available templates table. You can filter the table by the title of the templates. Then you need to click the #[i.fa.fa-eye.fa-lg.a-color] icon of the wanted template, the right side traveler preview will be updated, and the template row is highlighted. Click the "Use selected template" and confirm, and the template will be added to be traveler and become active.
            img(src='#{prefix}/images/use-form.png')
            p The new template will appear in the active template table, and the previously active template will appear in the used templates table. The change will be seem by all users.

          section#switch
            .page-header
              h2 Switch back to a used template
            p Sometimes, you might find one of the previously used templates is better than the current active one. You can easily switch by choosing the one you like in the "Used templates" table, and click the "Use selected template" button.
            img(src='#{prefix}/images/switch-form.png')
            p After switching, the active template and used templates table will be adjusted accordingly. The traveler update will be seen when it is loaded or refreshed.

          section#alias
            .page-header
              h2 Set the alias of a template
            p Every template that has been used by the traveler has an alias. When a template was first used by the traveler, the alias is the same as the template's title. You can update it by selecting it and click the "Set alias" button. The alias can help to distinguish templates.
            img(src='#{prefix}/images/form-alias.png')

          section#progress
            .page-header
              h2 The impact on the estimated traveler progress
            p The traveler progress is estimated by (number of finished inputs / total number of inputs). When the traveler template is changed, the total number of inputs will also be updated. However, the traveler updates the number of finished inputs only when the traveler is loaded with the collected data after the change. It is recommended that you load the traveler in a new browser window right after the template change in order to verify the change and also update the progress estimation.
